-- Simple VDM-SL template
-- This function adds two numbers together.
-- It demonstrates the basic structure of a VDM-SL function definition.

-- Functions in VDM-SL are defined with a name, a type signature, and a body.
-- The type signature specifies the input and output types.
-- 'nat' is the type of natural numbers (non-negative integers).

functions

    Add: nat * nat -> nat
    Add(a, b) ==
        a + b;